	(text "EEPROM WRITE PROTECT (EEPROM_nWP, J3 3-4)\nThe CM4 pulls EEPROM_nWP up internally (100k), so the\nbootloader EEPROM is writable unless J3 3-4 is fitted.\nThe jumper only takes effect once protection is enabled\nin the bootloader config (CM4 datasheet 2.18).\n\nProduction:\n- Set eeprom_write_protect=1 in the bootloader config\n  (via usbboot or rpi-eeprom-config) before shipping.\n- Fit the J3 3-4 jumper. The EEPROM is then protected\n  from power-up (CM4 datasheet 5.1).\n\nBootloader update:\n- Remove J3 3-4, update via usbboot or self-update,\n  then refit the jumper.\n\nWhy not a GPIO with a pull-down: CM4 EEPROM updates run\nonly via usbboot or bootloader self-update (datasheet\n6.3), before Linux can drive a GPIO, so the pin could\nnever be released for an update."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 231.14 84.455 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "342137f9-6d01-4fc1-9444-f251dee01ff6")
	)
	(text "H5/H6: optional I2C1 pull-ups, normally OPEN.\nCM4 already pulls GPIO2/3 up with 1.8k (DS p.7).\nFit both only for a long, high-capacitance bus\nat 400 kHz: ~1k total, ~2.9 mA sink at 0.4 V\n(I2C spec min 3 mA, so compliant devices are OK)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 187.452 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "372d484b-1e6c-47c1-8198-246722d57e13")
	)
	(text "I2C PULL-UPS\nI2C1: GPIO2 = I2C1_SDA (J4-16), GPIO3 = I2C1_SCL (J4-18)\nPulled up to 3.3 V (GPIO_VREF) by 1.8 kΩ inside the CM4\n(CM4 datasheet section 2.5, pins 56/58). No board pull-ups\nare needed. R20/R21 (2.2k, fitted via H5/H6) are optional.\n\nI2C0: GPIO0 = ID_SD (J4-22), GPIO1 = ID_SC (J4-23)\nNo I2C pull-ups on the CM4, only the BCM2711's weak reset\npull-ups (33-73 kΩ). If J4-22/23 are used as an I2C bus, the\ndevice on J4 must supply the pull-ups (2.2k-4.7k to 3.3 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "46118630-decc-4935-a2a7-ab48bf33e440")
	)
	(text "EEPROM write protect = Jumper Pins 3-4\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.838 59.182 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right bottom)
		)
		(uuid "47812c5e-b3cf-46a9-8acb-f25fa89ea43d")
	)
	(text "GPIO3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.902 79.248 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "49c52580-cdce-44c0-b079-b639903359fb")
	)
	(text "BOOT CONSOLE UART (J5): CM4 UART0, 3.3 V logic, 115200 baud, 8N1, no flow control\n  J5-1  BOOT_CONSOLE_RXD (GPIO15, CM4 receives)   <- adapter TXD\n  J5-2  BOOT_CONSOLE_TXD (GPIO14, CM4 transmits)  -> adapter RXD\n  J5-3  GND                                       -- adapter GND\nTX and RX cross over: the adapter TXD goes to the CM4 RXD.\n\nUse an inexpensive USB-to-TTL serial cable (PL2303 / CP2102 / FTDI type) with\nfemale jumper leads. Typical colours: black GND, white RXD, green TXD, red 5V.\nCheck the labels on your cable.\n\nDO NOT connect the adapter 5V lead. The board powers itself and J5 has no 5V pin.\nA loose 5V lead can short to the header or the board, so it is best to cut it off\n(or insulate it).\nUse an adapter with 3.3 V signals only. CM4 GPIOs are not 5 V tolerant: check that\nthe adapter TXD idles at about 3.3 V with a meter before connecting.\n\nLinux console: enable_uart=1 in config.txt (Pi OS cmdline.txt already has\nconsole=serial0,115200).\nBootloader messages: set BOOT_UART=1 in the EEPROM config (rpi-eeprom-config)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "59b5c7cd-9338-40a3-9b53-036619d169b0")
	)
	(text "AIN0 / AIN1 (J4-2 / J4-4), field wired, to CM4\nAnalogIP0/1 (MxL7704 ADC). Measures 0 to 2.55 V (8-bit).\nSurvives +/-24 V either polarity: R7/R6 10k series\n+ D4/D5 BAT54S clamps to GND and 3V3_CM4 (RCM4 sheet)\nhold the pins within -0.3 V / +3.6 V (abs max -0.3/+6.0).\nError: ADC input < 1 uA x 10k = 10 mV, plus clamp leakage\n(up to ~1-2 % hot). With the CM4 off, a driven input feeds\n< 0.3 mA (at 6 V) into 3V3_CM4 through the upper clamp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.626 138.176 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6117e5ac-d521-40e8-b2d3-ce9f741e644f")
	)
