	(text "Boot/EEPROM_EN/GLOBAL_EN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.178 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
		)
		(uuid "807e8285-9c1a-47ad-8cd7-d74550796211")
	)
	(text "POWER-CYCLE CONTROL (nPWR_CYCLE)\nLets the CM4 cut its own power after a clean shutdown and restart\nby itself. Use it when a normal reboot is not enough: it fully resets\nthe PMIC and all on-module power rails.\n\nHow it works:\n- GPIO6 drives U10 (74LVC1G07, open-drain). J3 pins 5-6 connect U10's\n  output to GLOBAL_EN (CM4 pin 99, 100k internal pull-up to 5V).\n- GPIO6 high (default pull-up at reset): U10 output is off and the\n  CM4 runs.\n- GPIO6 low: GLOBAL_EN is pulled low and the CM4 powers off.\n- U10 is powered from 3V3_CM4, which switches off with the CM4, so\n  U10 releases GLOBAL_EN and the CM4 powers back on.\n\nUse:\n- Fit the J3 5-6 jumper to enable. Fit J3 5-6 only after the \n  board and GPIO6 behaviour have been verified.\n- config.txt: dtoverlay=gpio-poweroff,gpiopin=6,active_low=1\n  \"sudo poweroff\" then shuts down cleanly and power-cycles the CM4.\n- Do not drive GPIO6 low while the OS is running. CM4 datasheet\n  section 2.13: pull GLOBAL_EN low only after the OS has shut down.\n- The datasheet needs GLOBAL_EN low for >1 ms. The low time here is\n  set by how fast 3V3_CM4 decays and is not guaranteed; check it with\n  a scope on first boards.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.812 98.552 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "89b36b0b-04e7-4b46-a8b2-e1bcf5587b40")
	)
	(text "GPIO8"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.902 71.374 0)
		(effects
