	)
	(text "GPIO0 / GPIO1 (J4-22 / J4-23)\nCM4 pins 36 (ID_SD = GPIO0) and 35 (ID_SC = GPIO1). This is the\nI2C0 bus the firmware normally uses to look for a HAT EEPROM and to\ncontrol CSI0/DSI0 cameras and displays. This board has no HAT, camera\nor display, so the pins are free for general use.\n\nTo use them as GPIO, add to config.txt (CM4 datasheet section 2.10):\n  force_eeprom_read=0\n  disable_poe_fan=1\nWithout these, the firmware drives the bus at boot to look for an\nEEPROM, and anything wired to these pins sees I2C activity.\n\n- Both pins are pulled up (high) at reset.\n- 3.3 V logic. Not 5 V tolerant.\n- They can also be used as an I2C bus (I2C0: GPIO0 = SDA,\n  GPIO1 = SCL). Add external pull-ups if you do.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 54.356 106.934 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f537e87d-afc5-4511-a9b6-9436cfc1d2e1")
	)
